<section class="section ground-inverse band" id="platform" aria-labelledby="platform-h"><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><h2 id="platform-h">NCS Nurse Call System runs on Sygnet IoT Connect. <span class="muted">The same platform under every Sygnet product.</span></h2></div>
<div class="grid grid--top"><div class="span-6 stack-5"><ol class="layers"><li><b>Device</b><span>Connect any device, sensor, machine or industrial system.</span></li><li><b>Edge</b><span>Run automation and process data locally, so sites keep working when the link drops.</span></li><li><b>Cloud</b><span>Store, manage and process device data on a secure platform.</span></li></ol><a class="link" href="/platform/">How the platform works</a></div>
<div class="span-6 start-7 stack-5"><p class="t-label muted">Used in</p><div class="chips"><a class="chip" href="/industries/healthcare/">Healthcare</a></div><p class="t-label muted">Related products</p><ul class="plist"><li><a class="plist__a" href="/products/queue-management-system/"><span class="plist__name">Sygnet QMS Queue Management System</span><span class="plist__one">Tokens by kiosk, QR or WhatsApp, with one dashboard for every branch.</span><svg class="m-arrow" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><path class="m-arrow__stem" d="M1 6h8"/><path class="m-arrow__head" d="M4.5 2.5 8 6l-3.5 3.5"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section " id="benefits" aria-labelledby="benefits-h">
<div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="benefits-h">Why hospitals install it. <span class="muted">Three things the ward feels.</span></h2></div><div class="grid grid--cards"><article class="card span-4 m-nolift"><h3>Staff performance you can see</h3><p>Each call is logged from press to attend, so nursing managers can review response by shift and by ward.</p></article><article class="card span-4 m-nolift"><h3>A calmer patient experience</h3><p>Patients know a call has gone through, and family members are not sent to look for a nurse.</p></article><article class="card span-4 m-nolift"><h3>Shorter turnaround and waiting</h3><p>Calls reach the nearest free nurse faster, so time between call and care comes down.</p></article></div></div>
</section>
<section class="section " id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
<div class="wrap"><div class="grid grid--top"><div class="span-5"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="faq-h">Questions about Nurse Call. <span class="muted">Answered from what we build today.</span></h2></div></div><div class="span-6 start-7"><div class="faq"><div class="faq__item"><h3>Is it wired or wireless?</h3><p>Both. Sygnet NCS is offered wired and wireless; the right one depends on the building and the number of beds.</p></div><div class="faq__item"><h3>Where does the reporting run?</h3><p>On a local server inside the hospital, alongside the nurse station display and the staff app.</p></div><div class="faq__item"><h3>Does it work with queue management?</h3><p>Yes. Hospitals can run Sygnet NCS and Sygnet QMS together on the Sygnet IoT Connect platform.</p></div></div></div></div></div>
</section>
